<edge source="us_china_trade_rivalry::supply_chain_diversity" target="global_rate_repricing::asset_allocation_tilt" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Greater geographic diversification of critical supply chains lowers concentration and earnings-volatility risk for corporates, reducing equity risk premia and prompting institutional investors to tilt portfolios toward equities and away from safe cash/bond holdings.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_trade_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">global_rate_repricing</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_trade_rivalry::supply_chain_diversity" target="mid_east_energy_shock::trade_rerouting_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Corporate moves to diversify supply chains away from China create new production and transshipment points, which directly increases the rate at which energy and goods shipments are re-routed to alternative sea lanes, hubs and logistics corridors.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_trade_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">mid_east_energy_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_trade_rivalry::supply_chain_diversity" target="russia_ukraine_war::sanction_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">When Western governments and firms materially diversify supply chains away from China, the reduced economic exposure lowers political risk of Chinese retaliation and makes governments more willing to impose or tighten coordinated trade and financial sanctions on Russia.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_trade_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
