  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">A marked rise in nominal yields (higher curve level) raises sovereign and corporate funding stress and market volatility, which market participants interpret as heightened economic fragility and elevate perceived geopolitical risk between major powers.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_rate_repricing</data>
