<edge source="global_rate_repricing::asset_allocation_tilt" target="ai_safety_militarization::deployment_rate_of_model" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Shifts by large investors toward equities and technology-heavy allocations lift public and private tech valuations and cash access for AI firms, enabling faster hiring, integration and rollout of trained models into production systems.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_rate_repricing</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_safety_militarization</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_rate_repricing::asset_allocation_tilt" target="us_china_trade_rivalry::chip_fab_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A tilt by institutional investors away from equities toward bonds/cash reduces availability and raises the cost of long-horizon equity and project finance, prompting delays, downsizing or cancellations of capital-intensive fab expansions and slowing near-term growth in operable capacity.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_rate_repricing</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_trade_rivalry</data>
</edge>
