<edge source="global_rate_repricing::cross_border_flows" target="ai_safety_militarization::capital_flow_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A drop in cross‑border capital flows (risk‑off/global repricing) directly reduces foreign portfolio, VC and FDI into major AI hubs, lowering the net rate of new investment available for AI development and commercialisation.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_rate_repricing</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_safety_militarization</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_rate_repricing::cross_border_flows" target="mid_east_energy_shock::crude_oil_supply_availab" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">An increase in cross‑border capital flows improves access to foreign financing, spare parts and offshore contractor services for exporters and refiners, sustaining production and exports and thus raising immediate crude availability.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_rate_repricing</data>
  <data key="d39">mid_east_energy_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_rate_repricing::cross_border_flows" target="russia_ukraine_war::defense_aid_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher cross‑border capital and banking flows ease financing, payment and logistics for procurement and transfers (including spare parts and munitions), directly increasing the rate and volume of defense aid that can be delivered to Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_rate_repricing</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_rate_repricing::cross_border_flows" target="us_china_trade_rivalry::cross_border_investment" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
